4.5.1. Beam search Beam search is a search heuristic that approximately maximizes the
total route probability under the network policy pθ(⋅|ϕ). It keeps a re­ cord, at each time step, a list of the nb most promising partial solutions sequences. From these candidates, beam search considers all admissible next visiting locations, and selects the best top-nb of them. When every beam reaches the final location, the solution with higher score is selected. When nb = 1, beam-search heuristic reduces to a simple greedy search. For beam search inference we show performance for nb ranging from 1 up to a maximum of 128 and finally consider performance and processing times for a maximum of 128 beams. Note that the number of beams cannot be higher than the number of nodes in the instance.

